━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ RowCapture is Tuple

` What a name a pattern binds to the case of a row of a table of unions stands for: the row's
` type, the number of the case, and whether TypeScript checked the row's storage where the
` pattern read it, as its cursor holds.

+ row TypeId
+ case-index U32
+ validated Bool

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ Arguments is Tuple

` A call site's arguments as the dispatcher sees them: the shape of each argument, its inferred
` type, its syntax, and any explicit type arguments. Where a value is piped into the call, `piped`
` is the call, which the argument piped has as its syntax. A markup element's call also gives its
` constructor the slots its body fills, each with the type of the builder it is given
` (`builders`), and the context of the styles the element sees (`context`).

+ shapes ImmutableArray'CallArgument'ArenaBacking
+ types ImmutableArray'TypeId'ArenaBacking
+ syntax ImmutableArray'SyntaxId'ArenaBacking
+ params ImmutableArray'TypeId'ArenaBacking
+ curried Bool = false
+ piped SyntaxId = 0
+ slots ImmutableArray'Atom'ArenaBacking = ImmutableArray'Atom'ArenaBacking()
+ builders ImmutableArray'TypeId'ArenaBacking = ImmutableArray'TypeId'ArenaBacking()
+ context U32 = U32.max

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ CallSite is Tuple

` The marks of a synthesized call site's runs on the scratch stacks.

+ shapes-mark ScratchMark
+ types-mark ScratchMark
+ syntax-mark ScratchMark
_ scratch TypingScratch

────────────────────
+ get shapes ImmutableArray'CallArgument'ArenaBacking

scratch.call-arguments.since(shapes-mark)

────────────────────
+ get types ImmutableArray'TypeId'ArenaBacking

scratch.types.since(types-mark)

────────────────────
+ get syntax ImmutableArray'SyntaxId'ArenaBacking

scratch.syntax.since(syntax-mark)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ ProtocolCall is Tuple

` A call of a method the compiler makes on a value without a call in the source: the call
` recorded, or none where the receiver has no such method, what the method answers, and the type
` it takes its argument as.

+ fact FactId = no-fact
+ answer TypeId = no-type
+ taken TypeId = no-type

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ Construction is Tuple

` A constructor a call has chosen, which the call interns once its arguments are settled
` (`intern-settled`), with what it gives the constructor apart from its arguments: the properties
` a markup element sets that name no parameter (`fills`), the context of the styles it sees, and
` the slots its body fills, each with the type of its builder.

+ module ModuleId = 0
+ decl DeclId = 0
+ receiver TypeId = no-type
+ fills Bool = false
+ context U32 = U32.max
+ slots ImmutableArray'Atom'ArenaBacking = ImmutableArray'Atom'ArenaBacking()
+ builders ImmutableArray'TypeId'ArenaBacking = ImmutableArray'TypeId'ArenaBacking()

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ Calls

+ frame Frame
+ host Demander? = null
+ conversions Conversions
+ ranking Ranking
_ delegator TypeId = no-type
_ interning RowCapture? = null
_ constructing Construction = Construction()
_ forward-row TypeId = no-type
_ unsettled-sites [SyntaxId]
_ unsettled-names [Atom]
_ unfound-sites [SyntaxId]
_ types Types
_ instances Instances
_ relations Relations
_ facts Facts
_ program Program
_ scratch TypingScratch
_ records-pairs = true

────────────────────
+ This
    - frame Frame
    - conversions Conversions

.. types = frame.types
.. relations = frame.relations
.. scratch = frame.scratch
.. instances = frame.instances
.. facts = frame.facts
.. program = frame.program
.. ranking = Ranking(frame.session, frame.module)

────────────────────
+ do begin

host = null
records-pairs = true
unsettled-sites.clear()
unsettled-names.clear()
unfound-sites.clear()
ranking.rebind(frame.module)

────────────────────
+ do attach
    - demander Demander

host = demander
ranking.host = demander
ranking.conversions = conversions
conversions.fitter = ranking

────────────────────
_ do note-outgoing
    - error TypeId
    - syntax SyntaxId

` An error leaving the function at a node, which the checker attached hears of first.
if host
    host.note-outgoing(error, syntax)
else
    frame.note-outgoing(error, syntax)

────────────────────
_ do defer-outgoing
    - callee InstanceId
    - syntax SyntaxId

if host
    host.defer-outgoing(callee, syntax)
else
    frame.defer-outgoing(callee, syntax)

────────────────────
_ do local-ranking Ranking
    - module ModuleId

` A ranking of its own, for a call ranked apart from the one being ranked, which has what is
` attached to type what it asks for.
. local = Ranking(frame.session, module)
local.host = host
local.conversions = if host then conversions else null
= local

────────────────────
+ do suspend-ranking Ranking?

` A ranking in the middle of a dispatch must not be reused: typing a closure argument can come
` back to this function for a lazy variable, whose value has calls of its own.
if !ranking.active
    = null
. busy = ranking
ranking = local-ranking(frame.module)
= busy

────────────────────
+ do resume-ranking
    - busy Ranking?

if busy
    ranking = busy

────────────────────
+ do function-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - name Atom
    - arguments Arguments

ranking.begin(arguments.shapes, arguments.types)
ranking.explicit-params(arguments.params)
. hit = ranking.dispatch-function(frame.self-type, name)
note-interface-call(frame.self-type, hit)
if hit && hit.receiver != no-type && hit.receiver != frame.self-type && !ranking.ambiguity()
    . delegated = ranking.delegates-to(frame.self-type, hit.receiver)
    if delegated
        delegator = frame.self-type
    if !delegated && intrinsic-is-class(types.completions[hit.receiver].intrinsic)
        conversions.convert(id, id, frame.self-type, hit.receiver, .reason-own-receiver)
if hit && hit.receiver != no-type && is-virtual-receiver(frame.self-type)
    instances.mark-may-panic(frame.instance)
if !hit && arguments.curried && ranking.partial
    . owner = ranking.partial.receiver
    . form = if owner == no-type then BindingForm.bound-function else BindingForm.bound-method
    = bind-partial(form, owner, arguments)
. callee = resolve-hit(id, .call-function, arguments.syntax, .function-not-found, hit, name, 0, frame.self-type, arguments.piped)
ranking.release()
if callee == no-instance
    = invalid-type
. answered = intrinsic-plan(callee)
if answered == .plan-count-leading-zeros && !counts-integer(callee)
    . message = "count-leading-zeros requires an integer argument"
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = invalid-type
if object-plan && types.intrinsic-of(instances.param-type(callee, 0)) != .class
    . message = "gc-object-from-pointer requires a class object type"
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = invalid-type
.. object-plan = answered == .plan-object-from-pointer
if witness-plan && types.intrinsic-of(instances.argument-type(callee, 0)) != .interface
    . message = "interface-witness-pointer requires an interface value"
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = invalid-type
.. witness-plan = answered == .plan-witness-pointer
if interface-plan && types.intrinsic-of(instances.param-type(callee, 0)) != .interface
    . message = "gc-interface-from-pointer requires an interface type"
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = invalid-type
.. interface-plan = answered == .plan-interface-from-pointer
if answered != .plan-side-payload && answered != .plan-publish-side-payload
    if answered != .plan-none
        facts.set-plan(frame.instance, id, answered)
    = demand-return(callee, id)
. returned = demand-return(callee, id)
. given = if returned != invalid-type && returned != no-type then returned else no-type
. payload = if answered == .plan-side-payload && given != no-type then unwrapped else given
    .. unwrapped = types.optional-inner(given)
if payload == no-type || types.intrinsic-of(payload) != .class
    . message = "GC object side payload intrinsics require a class payload type"
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = invalid-type
facts.set-plan(frame.instance, id, answered)
= returned

────────────────────
_ do stores-untraced Bool
    - callee InstanceId

` Whether a function is the one the arena module declares with no body for a pointer, which
` stores an item where the collector does not look. The compiler answers a call of it.
. row = instances.rows[callee]
if row.module != types.arena-module || row.self-type == no-type
    = false
if types.intrinsic-of(row.self-type) != .cpointer
    = false
. target = program.modules[row.module]
match? target.decls[row.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        if fn.owner == 0 || !fn.name || fn.name != types.store-untraced-atom!
            = false
        if fn.body == 0
            = true
        match? target.tree.nodes[fn.body]
            | .node-block(body)
                = body.body.count == 0
= false

────────────────────
+ do arena-traces Bool
    - type TypeId

` Whether a value of a type holds what an arena must tell the collector of: anything but
` numbers, text, atoms, pointers and the marks of a table, inside any tuple, struct, optional
` or case of a union that holds them.
if type == no-type || type == invalid-type
    = true
. completion = types.completion-of(type)
. kind = completion.intrinsic
if intrinsic-is-numeric(kind) || kind == .void || kind == .string || scalar
    = false
.. scalar = kind == .cpointer || kind == .bool || kind == .char
if kind == .atom || kind == .table-mark
    = false
if kind == .optional
    = arena-traces(types.optional-inner(type))
if kind == .union
    for fact in types.cases[completion.cases]
        if fact.type != no-type && arena-traces(fact.type)
            = true
    = false
if !intrinsic-is-tuple-like(kind)
    = true
. range = completion.properties
for offset in 0 .. < range.count
    if arena-traces(types.properties[range.start + offset].type)
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ counts-integer Bool
    - callee InstanceId

` Whether the one argument of a count of leading zeros is an integer.
counted != no-type && counted != invalid-type && integral

.. counted = instances.argument-type(callee, 0)
.. integral = is-integer-kind(types.completions[counted].intrinsic)

────────────────────
_ answered-in-place Bool
    - callee InstanceId

` Whether the compiler answers a call of the callee with no call of its own.
is-in-place-plan(intrinsic-plan(callee))

────────────────────
+ do intrinsic-plan OperatorPlan
    - callee InstanceId

` The plan of a call the compiler answers itself: of a function with no body that the
` intrinsics module declares, or of one of the four of the math module that take floats.
. row = instances.rows[callee]
. target = program.modules[row.module]
match? target.decls[row.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        if fn.body != 0 || !fn.name || fn.owner != 0
            = .plan-none
        . name = fn.name.text
        if row.module == types.intrinsics-module
            . written = fn.name
            if written == types.count-leading-zeros-atom!
                = .plan-count-leading-zeros
            if written == types.side-payload-atom!
                = .plan-side-payload
            if written == types.publish-side-payload-atom!
                = .plan-publish-side-payload
            if written == types.object-from-pointer-atom!
                = .plan-object-from-pointer
            if written == types.invoke-lowered-atom!
                instances.mark-may-panic(frame.instance)
                = .plan-invoke-lowered
            if written == types.witness-pointer-atom!
                = .plan-witness-pointer
            if written == types.interface-from-pointer-atom!
                = .plan-interface-from-pointer
        if target.name != "math"
            = .plan-none
        . signature = instances.signatures[callee]
        . float = types.type-row(.float64)
        for position in 0 .. < signature.args.count
            if instances.argument-type(callee, position) != float
                = .plan-none
        if name == "sqrt" && signature.args.count == 1
            = .plan-f64-sqrt
        if name == "abs" && signature.args.count == 1
            = .plan-f64-abs
        if name == "min" && signature.args.count == 2
            = .plan-f64-min
        if name == "max" && signature.args.count == 2
            = .plan-f64-max
= .plan-none

────────────────────
+ is-virtual-receiver Bool
    - receiver TypeId

` Whether a call on a receiver of this type is chosen by the class of the object: the type is
` a class written in source that some class is derived from. Such a call may panic whatever
` the function named does, because the one chosen may.
|? receiver == no-type || receiver == invalid-type
    false
|? completion.intrinsic != .class || completion.is-builtin
    false
??
    types.has-subclasses(receiver)

.. completion = types.completion-of(receiver)

────────────────────
+ do c-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - name Atom
    - arguments Arguments

ranking.begin(arguments.shapes, arguments.types)
ranking.explicit-params(arguments.params)
. hit = ranking.dispatch-c-function(name)
if !hit && arguments.curried && ranking.partial
    = bind-partial(.bound-c-function, no-type, arguments)
records-pairs = !name.text.starts-with("brix")
. callee = resolve-hit(id, .call-function, arguments.syntax, .function-not-found, hit, name, 0, no-type, arguments.piped)
records-pairs = true
ranking.release()
if callee == no-instance
    = invalid-type
if name == types.bench-collect-atom!
    facts.set-plan(frame.instance, id, .plan-elided)
note-described(id, name)
check-zone-call(id, name, callee)
check-claim(id, name)
= demand-return(callee, id)

────────────────────
_ do check-claim
    - id SyntaxId
    - name Atom

` A C function an effect claims is called only by a door of that effect, or by a function written
` in one. One that two effects claim is called by neither's.
. table = program.effects
=? if table.count == 0
. claimed = table.claims[name]
=? if !claimed
. contested = table.contested[name]
if contested
    . first = table.names[claimed].text
    . second = table.names[contested].text
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("'C:${name.text}' is claimed by both the '$first' and the '$second' effect"))
    =
. outer = frame.instance
while instances.rows[outer].enclosing != no-instance
    outer = instances.rows[outer].enclosing
. row = instances.rows[outer]
=? if table.door-of(row.module, row.decl) == claimed
. effect = table.names[claimed].text
frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("'C:${name.text}' belongs to the '$effect' effect, so only its doors may call it"))

────────────────────
_ do check-zone-call
    - id SyntaxId
    - name Atom
    - callee InstanceId

` A C call of a function that may suspend the task, where the code may not suspend, and one
` that may allocate from the collector, where the heap may not be used, are reported at the
` call: in a GC-free zone, naming where it is entered, or under `without suspend` or `without heap`.
` What a function may do is its claim (`claims.yumi`), and one that polls the collector and has
` none is taken to do both.
. polls = false
. row = instances.rows[callee]
match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        polls = (fn.effects /and/ CompilationEffect.gc-polling) != 0
if may-suspend(name.text, polls)
    frame.check-suspends(id)
if may-allocate(name.text, polls)
    frame.check-allocates(id)

────────────────────
_ do note-described
    - id SyntaxId
    - name Atom

` Plans a C call that allocates, resizes or copies the storage of an array the collector
` owns, with the type of the array's items. So too a call of an arena's own that reserves
` or copies storage for items of a type the arena traces, as TypeScript reserves and copies
` the storage of an `ArrayBuilder` an arena backs: the type is the parameter the function
` names `Value` or `Item`.
. item = no-type
if name == types.allocate-buffer-atom! || name == types.resize-buffer-atom! || slice-copy
    item = collected-item(frame.self-type)
.. slice-copy = name == types.copy-slice-atom!
if item == no-type && (name == types.arena-reserve-atom! || name == types.copy-slice-atom!)
    item = arena-item(frame.self-type)
if item != no-type && item != invalid-type && !types.completions[item].has-variables
    facts.set-constant(frame.instance, id, ConstantFact(item, 0, null, false), .plan-described)

────────────────────
_ arena-item TypeId
    - owner TypeId

` The type of the items an arena's function reserves storage for, where the arena traces
` them.
|? owner == no-type || owner == invalid-type || !types.is-arena(owner)
    no-type
|? item == no-type || item == invalid-type || !arena-traces(item)
    no-type
??
    item

.. item = types.env-lookup(frame.env, types.value-type-atom!) ?? types.env-lookup(frame.env, types.item-atom!) ?? no-type

────────────────────
_ do collected-item TypeId
    - owner TypeId

` The type of the items of the storage the functions of a class allocate from the collector:
` those of the backing that does so, for the type parameter the function names `Item`, and
` those of an array held by that backing.
if owner == no-type || owner == invalid-type || types.gc-backing-type == invalid-type
    = no-type
if owner == types.gc-backing-type
    = types.env-lookup(frame.env, types.item-atom!) ?? no-type
. immutable = types.ancestor-of(owner, types.immutable-array-decl)
. array = if immutable != no-type then immutable else types.ancestor-of(owner, types.array-decl)
if array == no-type
    = no-type
match? types.rows[array]
    | .type-class(row)
        if row.args.count == 2 && types.child-type(row.args, 1) == types.gc-backing-type
            = types.child-type(row.args, 0)
= no-type

────────────────────
+ do generator-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - callee InstanceId

` The one call of a comprehension's closure, passing the container: a closure call for the
` panic rules, with the callee's errors propagating like any call.
facts.record-call(frame.instance, id, callee, .call-closure, scratch.no-fills, false)
= demand-return(callee, id)

────────────────────
+ do slot-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - callee TypeId
    - arguments Arguments

if callee == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
if types.completions[callee].intrinsic == .binding
    = binding-call(id, callee, arguments)
if types.completions[callee].intrinsic == .closure
    if arguments.types.length < closure-arity(callee)
        = bind-values(.bound-closure, callee, arguments)
    . tail = closure-tail(callee)
    if tail != U32.max
        = tail-closure-call(id, callee, arguments, tail)
    . passed [TypeId]
    for position in 0 .. < arguments.types.length
        passed += closure-argument(callee, position, arguments)
    . given-mark = scratch.types.mark
    for type in passed
        scratch.types.push(type)
    . lambda = host!.demand-lambda(callee, scratch.types.since(given-mark))
    scratch.types.rewind(given-mark)
    if lambda == no-instance
        = invalid-type
    facts.record-call(frame.instance, id, lambda, .call-closure, scratch.no-fills, false)
    frame.forget-members()
    = demand-return(lambda, id)
= value-call(id, callee, RowRange'TypeId(), arguments)

────────────────────
+ do builder-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - builder TypeId
    - takes U32 = 0

` A call of what a value of a function type that takes `takes` arguments holds, which no call in
` the source writes, as a slot outlet calls the function that builds its slot: what it answers,
` each error the type carries leaving the function at the call, as at a call of such a value
` written in source. What runs is not known, so it may panic.
types.complete(builder)
. fn = function-row(types, builder)
if fn == no-type
    = invalid-type
. returns = no-type
. count U32
match? types.rows[fn]
    | .type-function(row)
        returns = row.return-type
        count = row.args.count
if count != takes
    = invalid-type
if !admits-value-call(id)
    = invalid-type
facts.record-call(frame.instance, id, no-instance, .call-closure, scratch.no-fills, false)
instances.mark-may-panic(frame.instance)
. carried = carried-result(types, builder)
if carried != no-type
    = raised-call(id, fn, carried)
= if returns == no-type then types.void-type else returns

────────────────────
_ do value-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - callee TypeId
    - held RowRange'TypeId
    - arguments Arguments

` Calls a value of a function type. Each argument takes a place the type declares: a named one
` the place of that name, the others the places left, in turn. A binding of the value holds
` the arguments given so far in their places, with the void type where a place is unfilled,
` and a call that leaves places unfilled gives such a binding. An argument of the void type
` fills its place as any other does. The call records which argument written fills each
` place, whether it calls or binds. An integer written with no suffix takes the type of its
` place. A type that carries errors answers with them, never with those of what the value
` holds.
types.complete(callee)
. fn = function-row(types, callee)
if fn == no-type
    frame.diagnose(id, .not-supported)
    = invalid-type
. args = RowRange'TypeId()
. returns = no-type
match? types.rows[fn]
    | .type-function(row)
        args = row.args
        returns = row.return-type
. unfilled = types.void-type
. places [TypeId]
. filled [Bool]
for offset in 0 .. < args.count
    . kept = if offset < held.count then types.child-type(held, offset) else unfilled
    places += kept
    filled += kept != unfilled
. names [Atom?]
declared-names(callee, names)
. order [U32]
. next = 0u32
for position in 0 .. < arguments.shapes.length
    while next < args.count && filled[next]
        next += 1
    . index = next
    . name = arguments.shapes[position].name
    if name
        . found = names.find(name)
        if found == null
            . message = program.store-atom("Unrecognized argument")
            frame.diagnose(arguments.syntax[position], .stated, message)
            = invalid-type
        index = found as U32
    if index >= args.count || filled[index]
        . message = program.store-atom("Wrong number of arguments")
        frame.diagnose(if name then arguments.syntax[position] else id, .stated, message)
        = invalid-type
    . declared = types.child-type(args, index)
    places[index] = conversions.adapted-literal
        - argument-expr(arguments.syntax[position])
        - arguments.types[position]
        - declared
    filled[index] = true
    order += index
. empty U32 = ArgumentFill.fill-empty
. fills-mark = scratch.words.mark
for place in 0 .. < args.count
    . written = order.find(place)
    scratch.words.push(if written then (written as U32) else empty)
. binds = filled.find(false) != null
if !binds && !admits-value-call(id)
    scratch.words.rewind(fills-mark)
    = invalid-type
facts.record-call
    - frame.instance
    - id
    - no-instance
    - .call-closure
    - scratch.words.since(fills-mark)
    - binds
scratch.words.rewind(fills-mark)
if binds
    . mark = scratch.types.mark
    for place in places
        scratch.types.push(place)
    = types.intern-binding(.bound-value, frame.module, 0, 0, callee, 0, mark)
frame.forget-members()
for offset in 0 .. < held.count
    . kept = types.child-type(held, offset)
    if kept != unfilled
        conversions.convert(id, id, kept, types.child-type(args, offset), .reason-argument)
for position in 0 .. < arguments.types.length
    . site = arguments.syntax[position]
    . declared = types.child-type(args, order[position])
    conversions.convert(site, site, places[order[position]], declared, .reason-argument)
. ref = class-ref(types, callee)
. steps = ref.module == types.generator-decl.module && ref.decl == types.generator-decl.decl
if steps && returns != no-type
    facts.set-plan(frame.instance, id, .plan-step)
    . stepped = types.optional-around(returns)
    . raised = step-result(types, callee, stepped)
    if raised != no-type
        = raised-call(id, callee, raised)
    = stepped
. carried = if steps then no-type else carried-result(types, callee)
if carried != no-type
    = raised-call(id, fn, carried)
= if returns == no-type then types.void-type else returns

────────────────────
_ do raised-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - function TypeId
    - carried TypeId

` What a call of a value of a function type that carries errors gives. Under `catch` it is
` the value or one of the errors. Elsewhere each error leaves the function at the call, and
` the call gives the value. What it answers with is kept for the type, for emission.
types.complete(carried)
facts.note-carried(function, carried)
if frame.surround.catch-depth != 0
    = carried
match? types.rows[carried]
    | .type-result(row)
        for offset in 0 .. < row.errors.count
            note-outgoing(types.child-type(row.errors, offset), id)
        facts.mark-propagates(frame.instance, id)
        = row.value
= carried

────────────────────
_ do declared-names
    - callee TypeId
    - names [Atom?]

` The names the arguments of a function type are called by, where the type is declared.
. level TypeId? = callee
while level
    match? types.rows[level]
        | .type-class(row)
            . owner = program.modules[row.module]
            match? owner.decls[row.decl]
                | .decl-class(class)
                    match? owner.tree.nodes[class.base]
                        | .node-type-function(fn)
                            for arg in owner.tree.children[fn.args]
                                names += declared-name(owner.tree, arg)
                            =
    level = types.base-of(level)

────────────────────
_ do declared-name Atom?
    - tree AST
    - arg SyntaxId

match? tree.nodes[arg]
    | .node-argument-decl(row)
        match? tree.nodes[row.pattern]
            | .node-type-capture(capture)
                match? tree.nodes[capture.id]
                    | .node-identifier(identifier)
                        = identifier.name
            | .node-identifier(identifier)
                = identifier.name
= null

────────────────────
+ do method-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - object-syntax SyntaxId
    - receiver TypeId
    - name Atom
    - arguments Arguments
    - written Bool = false
    - capture RowCapture? = null

` `written` marks a call the source spells as a method call, which a union must answer with
` every case's own method. A type given as a value is compared as the type it is known to be
` where the call stands, as it is when the type is named. A union a row of a table holds answers
` with each case's own method run on the row, as it is read where the row's storage was checked;
` there an extension of the case itself stands over one of a base of it.
. rows = forward-row
forward-row = no-type
if types.intrinsic-of(receiver) == .type-info && relates-types(name)
    = type-info-call(id, class-arg(types, receiver, 0), name, arguments)
ranking.begin(arguments.shapes, arguments.types)
ranking.explicit-params(arguments.params)
ranking.row-case = if capture then receiver else no-type
. hit = adapt-row(receiver, ranking.dispatch-method(receiver, name), capture)
note-interface-call(receiver, hit)
if !hit && !ranking.partial && types.intrinsic-of(receiver) == .union
    ranking.release()
    . gap = method-gap(receiver, name, arguments) if written
    if gap
        frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(gap), receiver)
        frame.mention(case-types(receiver))
        = invalid-type
    if forwards-to-cases(receiver)
        = forward-call(id, object-syntax, receiver, name, arguments, rows)
    frame.diagnose(id, .function-not-found, name)
    = invalid-type
. row = union-row(receiver)
if !hit && !ranking.partial && row != no-type
    ranking.release()
    forward-row = receiver
    = method-call(id, object-syntax, row, name, arguments, written)
. delegated = hit && ranking.delegates-to(receiver, hit.receiver)
if delegated
    delegator = receiver
. on-row = hit && capture && hit.receiver == capture.row
if hit && hit.receiver != receiver && !ranking.ambiguity() && !delegated && !on-row
    conversions.convert
        - object-syntax
        - object-syntax
        - receiver
        - hit.receiver
        - receiver-reason(id, object-syntax)
if hit && is-virtual-receiver(receiver)
    instances.mark-may-panic(frame.instance)
if !hit && arguments.curried && ranking.partial
    interning = null
    = bind-partial(.bound-method, receiver, arguments)
. callee = resolve-hit(id, .call-method, arguments.syntax, .function-not-found, hit, name, 0, receiver, arguments.piped)
interning = null
ranking.release()
if callee == no-instance
    = invalid-type
if stores-untraced(callee)
    . item = class-arg(types, instances.rows[callee].self-type, 0)
    . traced U64 = if arena-traces(item) then 1 else 0
    facts.set-constant
        - frame.instance
        - id
        - ConstantFact(traced, 0, null, false)
        - .plan-store-untraced
. returned = demand-return(callee, id)
if types.intrinsic-of(receiver) == .type-relation && arguments.types.length == 1
    . named = facts.relation-at(frame.instance, object-syntax)
    if named != no-fact && (name.text == "cast" || name.text == "unify")
        = relation-cast(id, facts.relations[named], arguments.types[0], arguments.syntax[0])
= returned

────────────────────
_ do relation-cast TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - named RelationFact
    - value TypeId
    - given SyntaxId

` The relation of two types converts a value by itself: its `cast` gives the value as the type
` the relation leads to, and a relation that is not legal refuses the value. The call is
` planned as one the compiler answers, and what converts the value is recorded at the value.
` A relation of two types that share an equal unit converts in two steps: to the type the
` first converts to, and from that by the ratio. A value that is not of the type the relation
` starts at is the receiver of the converter where the relation is one, and converts to that
` type first, as a receiver does; under any other relation it has nothing recorded, and
` emission refuses it. An integer written with no suffix that fits the type it starts at is of that
` type.
. relation = relations.compare(named.from, named.to, named.unifies, false, null, frame.module)
if !relation-legal(relation)
    frame.diagnose(id, .illegal-cast, null, named.from, named.to)
    = invalid-type
facts.set-plan(frame.instance, id, .plan-relation-cast)
. held = conversions.adapted-literal(argument-site(given), value, named.from)
if relation.kind == .relation-same
    = held
. target = if named.unifies && relation.unified != no-type then relation.unified else relation.to
if held == named.from
    . fitted = if types.is-optional(target) then types.optional-inner(target) else target
    conversions.check-literal-fit(argument-site(given), fitted)
    if relation.kind == .relation-common-equality && relation.via != no-type
        convert-related(given, held, relation.via)
        convert-related(given, relation.via, target)
    else
        convert-related(given, held, target)
else if relation.kind == .relation-converter
    . received = relations.compare(held, named.from, false, false, null, frame.module)
    if !relation-legal(received)
        frame.diagnose(given, .illegal-cast, null, held, named.from)
        = invalid-type
    conversions.check-literal-fit(argument-site(given), named.from)
    conversions.record-conversion(given, received, .reason-relation)
    convert-related(given, named.from, target)
= target

────────────────────
_ do convert-related
    - given SyntaxId
    - from TypeId
    - to TypeId

` Records at a value what converts it from one type to another, for a relation asked to
` cast it. Nothing is recorded where the two are one type or do not convert.
. found = relations.compare(from, to, false, false, null, frame.module)
if relation-legal(found) && found.kind != .relation-same
    conversions.record-conversion(given, found, .reason-relation)

────────────────────
_ do note-relation
    - id SyntaxId
    - from TypeId
    - to TypeId
    - unifies Bool

` Plans a relation asked of a type as one the compiler answers, and records the text it is
` printed as: its name, and the names of the two types as they are when the program runs.
if from == no-type || from == invalid-type || to == no-type || to == invalid-type
    =
. relation = relations.compare(from, to, unifies, false, null, frame.module)
. left = type-runtime-name(types, from)
. right = type-runtime-name(types, to)
. shown = "[${relation-name(relation.kind)} $left = $right]"
facts.set-constant
    - frame.instance
    - id
    - ConstantFact(0, 0, program.store-atom(shown), false)
    - .plan-relation

────────────────────
+ union-row TypeId
    - receiver TypeId

row-union(types, receiver)

────────────────────
+ do has-method Bool
    - receiver TypeId
    - name Atom
    - arguments Arguments

` Whether a method of the receiver takes these arguments, in full or in part.
ranking.begin(arguments.shapes, arguments.types)
ranking.explicit-params(arguments.params)
. found = ranking.dispatch-method(receiver, name) != null || ranking.partial != null
ranking.release()
= found

────────────────────
+ do has-getter Bool
    - receiver TypeId
    - name Atom

` Whether a getter answers the name: one an extension adds is no property of the class.
. site = open-site()
ranking.begin(site.shapes, site.types)
. found = ranking.dispatch-getter(receiver, name)
ranking.release()
close-site(site)
= found != null

────────────────────
+ do has-setter Bool
    - receiver TypeId
    - name Atom
    - value TypeId
    - rhs SyntaxId

` Whether a setter takes the value for the name: one an extension adds is no property of the class.
. site = open-site()
push-argument(value, rhs)
ranking.begin(site.shapes, site.types)
. found = ranking.dispatch-setter(receiver, name)
ranking.release()
close-site(site)
= found != null

────────────────────
_ do method-gap String?
    - union TypeId
    - name Atom
    - arguments Arguments

` Why a union cannot answer a method with its cases' own: the first case that holds no value,
` or whose value has no method taking the arguments in full.
for index in 0 .. < types.cases-of(union).length
    . fact = types.cases-of(union)[index]
    if fact.is-default || fact.type == no-type || fact.type == invalid-type
        = gap-text(fact, index, "no payload", "method", name)
    ranking.begin(arguments.shapes, arguments.types)
    ranking.explicit-params(arguments.params)
    . found = ranking.dispatch-method(fact.type, name) != null
    ranking.release()
    if !found && !forwards-to-cases(fact.type)
        = gap-text(fact, index, "no complete dispatch", "method", name)
= null

────────────────────
+ do getter-gap String?
    - union TypeId
    - name Atom

` Why a union cannot answer a property with its cases' own.
for index in 0 .. < types.cases-of(union).length
    . fact = types.cases-of(union)[index]
    if fact.is-default || fact.type == no-type || fact.type == invalid-type
        = gap-text(fact, index, "no payload", "getter", name)
    if types.property-named(fact.type, name) == null && !has-getter(fact.type, name)
        = gap-text(fact, index, "no complete dispatch", "getter", name)
= null

────────────────────
_ gap-text String
    - fact TypeCase
    - index Size
    - lack String
    - member String
    - name Atom

"Union case $shown has $lack for $member '${name.text}'"

.. shown = if fact.name then "'${fact.name.text}'" else "#$index (${type-display(types, fact.type)})"

────────────────────
+ do case-types [TypeId]
    - union TypeId

. found [TypeId]
for fact in types.cases-of(union)
    found += fact.type
= found

────────────────────
+ do forwards-to-cases Bool
    - receiver TypeId

` A union whose every case holds a value answers a member it does not declare with each
` case's own.
if types.intrinsic-of(receiver) != .union
    = false
. cases = types.cases-of(receiver)
for fact in cases
    if fact.is-default || fact.type == no-type || fact.type == invalid-type
        = false
= cases.length != 0

────────────────────
_ do forward-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - object-syntax SyntaxId
    - receiver TypeId
    - name Atom
    - arguments Arguments
    - row TypeId = no-type

. results [TypeId]
for index in 0 .. < types.cases-of(receiver).length
    . payload = types.cases-of(receiver)[index].type
    . capture = if row != no-type then RowCapture(row, index as U32, true) else null
    . returned = method-call(id, object-syntax, payload, name, arguments, false, capture)
    if returned == invalid-type
        = invalid-type
    if results.find(returned) == null
        results += returned
facts.set-plan(frame.instance, id, .plan-forward)
= forward-results(id, results)

────────────────────
+ do forward-results TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - results [TypeId]

` What a member a union forwards gives, with the conversion of what each case gives to it
` recorded at the node, where the cases give more than one type and no error.
. joined = forwarded-type(results)
facts.note-forward(frame.instance, id, joined)
if results.length == 1 || joined == invalid-type || types.intrinsic-of(joined) != .union
    = joined
for result in results
    if result != joined
        conversions.convert(id, id, result, joined, .reason-join)
= joined

────────────────────
+ do forwarded-type TypeId
    - results [TypeId]

` What a forwarded member gives: the one type every case gives, or the union of them, raising
` every error any case raises.
if results.length == 1
    = results[0]
. values [TypeId]
. errors [TypeId]
for result in results
    . value = result
    match? types.rows[result]
        | .type-result(row)
            value = row.value
            for offset in 0 .. < row.errors.count
                . error = types.child-type(row.errors, offset)
                if errors.find(error) == null
                    errors += error
    if values.find(value) == null
        values += value
. joined = values[0]
if values.length != 1
    . mark = scratch.types.mark
    for value in values
        scratch.types.push(value)
    joined = types.intern-union(mark)
if errors.length == 0
    = joined
. raised = scratch.types.mark
for error in errors
    scratch.types.push(error)
= result-type(types, joined, raised)

────────────────────
+ do c-binding TypeId
    - name Atom

` A C function read as a value binds no arguments yet.
. site = open-site()
ranking.begin(site.shapes, site.types)
. hit = ranking.dispatch-c-function(name)
. candidate = hit ?? ranking.partial
. result = no-type
if candidate
    result = types.intern-binding(.bound-c-function, frame.module, candidate.module, candidate.decl)
ranking.release()
close-site(site)
= result

────────────────────
+ do method-binding TypeId
    - receiver TypeId
    - name Atom
    - read SyntaxId = 0

` A method read as a value binds its receiver: no arguments yet, so every overload that still
` wants some is a candidate. Read at a node, it binds as the reference does each parameter
` from the first that is written with a default, to the default evaluated there; a method
` that wants an argument before its last such parameter is not supported.
. site = open-site()
ranking.begin(site.shapes, site.types)
. hit = ranking.dispatch-method(receiver, name)
. candidate = hit ?? ranking.partial
. result = no-type
. leading = if candidate && read != 0 then leading-defaults(candidate.module, candidate.decl) else 0u32
if candidate && leading == 0
    result = types.intern-binding
        - .bound-method
        - frame.module
        - candidate.module
        - candidate.decl
        - receiver
else if candidate && !hit
    frame.diagnose(read, .not-supported)
    result = invalid-type
else if hit
    result = bind-defaults(hit, receiver, leading, read)
ranking.release()
close-site(site)
= result

────────────────────
_ do leading-defaults U32
    - module ModuleId
    - decl DeclId

` How many parameters of a function, from the first, are written with a default.
. owner = program.modules[module]
. count = 0u32
match? owner.decls[decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        while count < fn.args.count && owner.arg-pool[fn.args.start + count].default-syntax != 0
            count += 1
= count

────────────────────
_ do bind-defaults TypeId
    - hit Hit
    - receiver TypeId
    - leading U32
    - read SyntaxId

` The binding a method read as a value makes of its receiver and the first parameters it is
` written with defaults for, each held as the parameter's type. The method as called with
` none given is recorded at the read, with each default's conversion, as a call that leaves
` them out records them.
. callee = intern-settled(hit, callee-effects(frame, hit.module, hit.decl))
host!.demand(callee)
. mark = scratch.types.mark
for position in 0 .. < leading
    scratch.types.push(hit.args[position as Size])
. result = types.intern-binding
    - .bound-method
    - frame.module
    - hit.module
    - hit.decl
    - receiver
    - 0
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
for position in 0 .. < leading
    convert-default(read, hit, callee, position, false)
do facts.record-call(frame.instance, read, callee, .call-method, scratch.no-fills, true)
= result

────────────────────
_ do bind-partial TypeId
    - form BindingForm
    - object TypeId
    - arguments Arguments

` The binding a curried call leaves when it gives its callee too few arguments: the candidate
` it partly matched, with the explicit type arguments and the argument types given so far. An
` integer written with no suffix is held as the type of the parameter it fills.
. partial = ranking.partial!
. module = partial.module
. decl = partial.decl
. adapted [TypeId]
for type in arguments.types
    adapted += type
for slot in 0 .. < partial.fills.length
    . filled = partial.fills[slot] as Size
    if filled < adapted.length && slot < partial.args.length
        . expr = argument-expr(arguments.syntax[filled])
        adapted[filled] = conversions.adapted-literal(expr, adapted[filled], partial.args[slot])
ranking.release()
. mark = scratch.types.mark
for type in adapted
    scratch.types.push(type)
. held = Arguments
    - arguments.shapes
    - scratch.types.since(mark)
    - arguments.syntax
    - arguments.params
    - arguments.curried
. result = bind-values(form, object, held, module, decl)
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
= result

────────────────────
_ do bind-values TypeId
    - form BindingForm
    - object TypeId
    - arguments Arguments
    - module ModuleId = 0
    - decl DeclId = 0

. mark = scratch.types.mark
for param in arguments.params
    scratch.types.push(param)
for type in arguments.types
    scratch.types.push(type)
. count U32 = arguments.params.length as U32
= types.intern-binding(form, ranking.caller, module, decl, object, count, mark)

────────────────────
_ do closure-arity Size
    - closure TypeId

match? types.rows[closure]
    | .type-closure(row)
        match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
            | .decl-function(fn)
                = fn.args.count
= 0

────────────────────
_ do closure-tail U32
    - closure TypeId

match? types.rows[closure]
    | .type-closure(row)
        match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
            | .decl-function(fn)
                = fn.variadic-index
= U32.max

────────────────────
_ do closure-signature Signature
    - closure TypeId

. module = 0u32
. decl = 0u32
match? types.rows[closure]
    | .type-closure(row)
        module = row.module
        decl = row.decl
= signature-into(types, module, decl, no-type-arguments(types), no-type, true)

────────────────────
_ do closure-argument TypeId
    - closure TypeId
    - position Size
    - arguments Arguments

` The type a nested function is typed for at an argument written before any tail: the type
` its parameter states, which the argument converts to at the call as TypeScript converts
` it, or the argument's own where the parameter states none, or states a union or a type
` with variables.
. given = arguments.types[position]
. plain = closure-signature(closure)
if position >= plain.args.length
    = given
. declared = plain.args[position]
if declared == given || declared == invalid-type || declared == no-type
    = given
if types.completions[declared].has-variables || types.completions[declared].intrinsic == .or
    = given
. stated = false
match? types.rows[closure]
    | .type-closure(row)
        match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
            | .decl-function(fn)
                if position < fn.args.count
                    stated = program.modules[row.module].arg-pool[fn.args.start + position].type-syntax != 0
if !stated
    = given
. site = arguments.syntax[position]
conversions.check-literal-fit(argument-site(site), declared)
conversions.convert(site, site, given, declared, .reason-argument)
= declared

────────────────────
_ do tail-closure-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - callee TypeId
    - arguments Arguments
    - tail U32

` A call of a nested function whose last parameter is a variadic tail, which TypeScript packs as a
` function's call packs its tail: the arguments from the tail on are made a list of the item the
` tail declares, or where it declares none of the union of the distinct types they give, in order,
` each converted to the item. The nested function is typed for the arguments before the tail and the
` list.
for shape in arguments.shapes
    if shape.name || shape.is-optional
        frame.diagnose(id, .not-supported)
        = invalid-type
. first = tail as Size
. variadic U32 = ArgumentFill.fill-variadic
. plain = closure-signature(callee)
. declared = if first < plain.args.length then plain.args[first] else invalid-type
. item = invalid-type
if declared != invalid-type && !types.completions[declared].has-variables
    match? types.rows[declared]
        | .type-class(row)
            if row.module == types.list-decl.module && row.decl == types.list-decl.decl && has-args
                item = types.child-type(row.args, 0)
            .. has-args = row.args.count >= 1
else
    . distinct [TypeId]
    for position in first .. < arguments.types.length
        if distinct.find(arguments.types[position]) == null
            distinct += arguments.types[position]
    if distinct.length == 1
        item = distinct[0]
    else if distinct.length != 0
        . mark = scratch.types.mark
        for type in distinct
            scratch.types.push(type)
        item = types.intern-union(mark)
if item == invalid-type || item == no-type
    frame.diagnose(id, .not-supported)
    = invalid-type
. list-mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(item)
. list = types.class-with-args(types.list-decl.module, types.list-decl.decl, list-mark)
for position in first .. < arguments.types.length
    . site = arguments.syntax[position]
    conversions.check-literal-fit(argument-site(site), item)
    if arguments.types[position] != item
        conversions.convert(site, site, arguments.types[position], item, .reason-element)
. passed [TypeId]
for position in 0 .. < first
    passed += closure-argument(callee, position, arguments)
. given-mark = scratch.types.mark
for type in passed
    scratch.types.push(type)
scratch.types.push(list)
. lambda = host!.demand-lambda(callee, scratch.types.since(given-mark))
scratch.types.rewind(given-mark)
if lambda == no-instance
    = invalid-type
note-list(id, list)
. fills-mark = scratch.words.mark
for position in 0 .. < tail
    scratch.words.push(position)
scratch.words.push(variadic)
facts.record-call(frame.instance, id, lambda, .call-closure, scratch.words.since(fills-mark), false)
scratch.words.rewind(fills-mark)
frame.forget-members()
= demand-return(lambda, id)

────────────────────
_ do binding-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - callee TypeId
    - arguments Arguments

` A call of a binding passes the arguments it holds and then the call's own, to whatever its
` form names. Too few arguments under a curried call leave a further binding. A binding of
` the constructor a tuple or struct is given takes its parameters and no argument: the
` fields it does not hold take their defaults.
. form = BindingForm.bound-function
. scope = frame.module
. module = 0u32
. decl = 0u32
. object = no-type
. param-count = 0u32
. items = RowRange'TypeId()
match? types.rows[callee]
    | .type-binding(row)
        form = row.form
        scope = row.scope
        module = row.module
        decl = row.decl
        object = row.object
        param-count = row.param-count
        items = row.items
if form == .bound-value
    = value-call(id, object, items, arguments)
if form == .bound-constructor && arguments.types.length != 0 && is-made-constructor(module, decl)
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Illegal arguments to binding"))
    = invalid-type
. params-start = scratch.types.mark
. given = 0
for offset in 0 .. < param-count
    scratch.types.push(types.child-type(items, offset))
    given += 1
for param in arguments.params
    scratch.types.push(param)
    given += 1
. site = open-site()
for offset in param-count .. < items.count
    push-argument(types.child-type(items, offset), id)
for position in 0 .. < arguments.types.length
    scratch.call-arguments.push(arguments.shapes[position])
    scratch.types.push(arguments.types[position])
    scratch.syntax.push(arguments.syntax[position])
. params = scratch.types.span(params-start, given)
. combined = Arguments
    - site.shapes
    - site.types
    - site.syntax
    - params
    - arguments.curried
    - arguments.piped
    - arguments.slots
    - arguments.builders
    - arguments.context
. diagnosed = facts.diagnostics.length
. result = call-bound(id, form, scope, module, decl, object, combined)
if result == invalid-type
    . message = program.store-atom("Illegal arguments to binding")
    facts.restate(diagnosed, frame.instance, id, .function-not-found, .stated, message)
    facts.restate(diagnosed, frame.instance, id, .constructor-not-found, .stated, message)
close-site(site)
scratch.types.rewind(params-start)
= result

────────────────────
+ do bound-return BoundReturn
    - binding TypeId
    - args ImmutableArray'TypeId'ArenaBacking
    - asked Bool = false

` The type a binding returns for these argument types, which a parameter of a function type
` infers from, with the function, the method or the constructor it calls with them. Nothing is
` reported: a binding that does not take them returns the invalid type, and so does one of a
` function or a method they leave a parameter of.
. form = BindingForm.bound-function
. scope = frame.module
. module = 0u32
. decl = 0u32
. object = no-type
. param-count = 0u32
. items = RowRange'TypeId()
match? types.rows[binding]
    | .type-binding(row)
        form = row.form
        scope = row.scope
        module = row.module
        decl = row.decl
        object = row.object
        param-count = row.param-count
        items = row.items
. shapes-mark = scratch.call-arguments.mark
. types-mark = scratch.types.mark
for offset in param-count .. < items.count
    scratch.call-arguments.push(CallArgument(null, false, false, false, false))
    scratch.types.push(types.child-type(items, offset))
for type in args
    scratch.call-arguments.push(CallArgument(null, false, false, false, false))
    scratch.types.push(type)
. given = scratch.types.since(types-mark)
. result = BoundReturn()
if form == .bound-closure
    . returned = lambda-return(host!, instances, object, given)
    if returned != invalid-type
        result = BoundReturn(returned, host!.demand-lambda(object, given))
else if form == .bound-value
    match? types.rows[function-row(types, object)]
        | .type-function(row)
            result = BoundReturn(row.return-type)
else
    . shapes = scratch.call-arguments.since(shapes-mark)
    result = settle-bound(form, scope, module, decl, object, shapes, given, asked)
scratch.types.rewind(types-mark)
scratch.call-arguments.rewind(shapes-mark)
= result

────────────────────
_ do settle-bound BoundReturn
    - form BindingForm
    - scope ModuleId
    - module ModuleId
    - decl DeclId
    - object TypeId
    - shapes ImmutableArray'CallArgument'ArenaBacking
    - given ImmutableArray'TypeId'ArenaBacking
    - asked Bool

. name Atom? = null
match? program.modules[module].decls[decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        name = fn.name
. local = local-ranking(scope)
local.asked = asked
local.begin(shapes, given)
. hit Hit? = null
if form == .bound-constructor
    local.bound-call = true
    hit = local.dispatch-constructor(object, true)
else if name && form == .bound-method
    hit = local.dispatch-method(object, name)
else if name && form == .bound-c-function
    hit = local.dispatch-c-function(name)
else if name
    hit = local.dispatch-function(frame.self-type, name)
. result = BoundReturn()
. whole = !hit || constructs || c-function || takes-every(hit.module, hit.decl, given.length)
    .. constructs = form == .bound-constructor
    .. c-function = form == .bound-c-function
if hit && whole
    . callee = intern-settled(hit, callee-effects(frame, hit.module, hit.decl))
    host!.demand(callee)
    . signature = instances.signatures[callee]
    . returned = signature.returns
    if form == .bound-constructor
        returned = hit.receiver
    else if signature.return-state == .return-pending
        returned = invalid-type
    result = BoundReturn(returned, callee)
local.release()
= result

────────────────────
_ do takes-every Bool
    - module ModuleId
    - decl DeclId
    - count Size

` Whether a function a binding calls as a value of a function type is given every parameter,
` as the reference requires: a default is no part of the call, and only a variadic tail
` takes any number.
match? program.modules[module].decls[decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        = fn.variadic-index != U32.max || fn.args.count as Size == count
= true

────────────────────
_ do call-bound TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - form BindingForm
    - scope ModuleId
    - module ModuleId
    - decl DeclId
    - object TypeId
    - arguments Arguments

. name Atom? = null
match? program.modules[module].decls[decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        name = fn.name
match form
    |= .bound-constructor
        = construction-on(id, with-params(object, arguments.params), arguments, true, 0, true)
    |= .bound-closure
        if arguments.types.length < closure-arity(object)
            frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Bound function not found"))
            = invalid-type
        = slot-call(id, object, arguments)
    ??
        if !name
            frame.diagnose(id, .function-not-found)
            = invalid-type
        . caller = ranking.caller
        ranking.caller = scope
        . result = bound-dispatch(id, form, object, name, arguments)
        ranking.caller = caller
        = result

────────────────────
_ do bound-dispatch TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - form BindingForm
    - object TypeId
    - name Atom
    - arguments Arguments

` A binding of a function, a method or a C function chooses among the overloads of the module
` it was made in, which the ranking looks them up from.
if form == .bound-method
    = method-call(id, id, object, name, arguments)
if form == .bound-c-function
    = c-call(id, name, arguments)
= function-call(id, name, arguments)

────────────────────
_ do explain-rows
    - receiver TypeId
    - arguments Arguments
    - by-name Bool
    - diagnosed Size

` Where a constructor matches nothing but would were each value cast, the first value of a row of
` its tail, such as a bullet, that converts only when asked is reported in place of the call.
ranking.begin(arguments.shapes, arguments.types)
ranking.asked = true
. hit = ranking.dispatch-constructor(receiver, by-name)
ranking.asked = false
. fills [U32]
. wanted [TypeId]
if hit
    for offset in 0 .. < hit.tail-fills.length
        fills += hit.tail-fills[offset]
        wanted += hit.tail-relations[offset].to
ranking.release()
for offset in 0 .. < fills.length
    . fill = fills[offset] as Size
    . target = if arguments.shapes[fill].name then value-field(wanted[offset]) else wanted[offset]
    if target != no-type && explain-row(argument-expr(arguments.syntax[fill]), target, diagnosed)
        =

────────────────────
_ do value-field TypeId
    - pair TypeId

` What a row written with a name gives its value as: the last field of the tuple the row is.
types.complete(pair)
. mark = types.scratch.types.mark
push-fields(types, pair)
. count = types.scratch.types.length - mark
. field = if count == 2 then types.scratch.types[mark + 1] else no-type
types.scratch.types.rewind(mark)
= field

────────────────────
_ do explain-row Bool
    - item SyntaxId
    - wanted TypeId
    - diagnosed Size

` Whether a value of a row converts only when asked to what it is wanted as, reported where it
` is written, or where a tuple written is wanted as a tuple, at the first of its items that does.
=? false if conversions.fits-unasked(item, wanted)
match? frame.tree.nodes[item]
    | .node-tuple-syntax(row)
        types.complete(wanted)
        . mark = types.scratch.types.mark
        push-fields(types, wanted)
        . fields [TypeId]
        for offset in mark .. < types.scratch.types.length
            fields += types.scratch.types[offset]
        types.scratch.types.rewind(mark)
        if fields.length == row.items.count
            . offset = 0
            for element in frame.tree.children[row.items]
                =? true if explain-row(element, fields[offset], diagnosed)
                offset += 1
. value = facts.node-type(frame.instance, item)
=? false if value == no-type || value == invalid-type
=? false if !relation-legal(relations.compare-explicit(value, wanted))
facts.diagnostics.truncate(diagnosed)
conversions.convert(item, item, value, wanted, .reason-argument)
= true

────────────────────
_ do is-made-constructor Bool
    - module ModuleId
    - decl DeclId

match? program.modules[module].decls[decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        = fn.is-generated && implicit
            .. implicit = fn.kind == .default-constructor-decl || fn.kind == .tuple-constructor-decl
= false

────────────────────
_ do recast-property DeclId
    - hit Hit
    - position Size
    - expected TypeId

` The property a constructor the compiler generates for a tuple or struct with type
` parameters fills from an argument, where the property holds a value of a function type
` and is declared with a type that names one of the parameters. The reference gives such
` an argument the function type with no name, and makes the property's type of it where
` the property is declared. No property for any other argument.
match? program.modules[hit.module].decls[hit.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        . params = types.class-type-args(hit.module, fn.owner)
        if !fn.is-generated || fn.kind != .tuple-constructor-decl || params.count == 0
            = 0
        . held = types.optional-inner(expected)
        types.complete(held)
        . plain = function-row(types, held)
        . ref = class-ref(types, held)
        . steps = ref.module == types.generator-decl.module && ref.decl == types.generator-decl.decl
        if plain == no-type || plain == held || steps || is-c-function(types, held)
            = 0
        . filled = 0
        for property in types.properties-of(hit.receiver)
            if property.slot == U32.max
                continue
            if filled == position
                . declared = owner-property(program, hit.module, fn.owner, property.name)
                = if names-parameter(hit.module, params, declared) then declared else 0
            filled += 1
= 0

────────────────────
_ do names-parameter Bool
    - module ModuleId
    - params RowRange'SyntaxId
    - property DeclId

` Whether the type a property is declared with names one of its class's type parameters.
if property == 0
    = false
. tree = program.modules[module].tree
match? program.modules[module].decls[property]
    | .decl-property(row)
        if row.type-syntax == 0
            = false
        for id in tree.subtree-start(row.type-syntax) .. < row.type-syntax + 1
            . name = types.type-syntax-name(tree, id)
            for position in 0 .. < params.count
                if name && types.class-param-name(tree, params, position) == name
                    = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do convert-recast
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - given TypeId
    - expected TypeId
    - callee InstanceId
    - property DeclId

` Converts an argument of a generated constructor to a property that `recast-property`
` names, as the reference does: to the function type with no name, then to the property's
` type by the function made for the two, which is placed where the property is declared,
` and then to the optional that holds it. An optional given has no shape here.
. named = types.optional-inner(expected)
. plain = function-row(types, named)
. kind = types.completions[given].intrinsic
if types.is-optional(given) || (kind != .closure && kind != .binding && kind != .function)
    frame.diagnose(syntax, .not-supported)
    =
if differs && conversions.convert(syntax, syntax, given, plain, .reason-argument) == invalid-type
    =
.. differs = given != plain
match? program.modules[instances.rows[callee].module].decls[property]
    | .decl-property(row)
        facts.place-cast(plain, named, callee, row.syntax)
conversions.convert(syntax, syntax, plain, named, .reason-argument)
if named != expected
    conversions.convert(syntax, syntax, named, expected, .reason-argument)

────────────────────
_ do holds-callable Bool
    - given TypeId
    - expected TypeId

` Whether an argument is a closure or a binding given where an optional of a function type
` is wanted: it becomes a value of the function type first, and then what holds it.
. kind = types.completions[given].intrinsic
if (kind != .closure && kind != .binding) || !types.is-optional(expected)
    = false
. inner = types.optional-inner(expected)
types.complete(inner)
= function-row(types, inner) != no-type

────────────────────
_ do with-params TypeId
    - object TypeId
    - params ImmutableArray'TypeId'ArenaBacking

` The class a bound constructor constructs once its call names the type parameters.
if params.length == 0
    = object
match? types.rows[object]
    | .type-class(row)
        . mark = scratch.types.mark
        for param in params
            scratch.types.push(param)
        = types.class-pattern-with-args(row.module, row.decl, mark)
= object

────────────────────
+ do static-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - owner TypeId
    - name Atom
    - arguments Arguments

if types.intrinsic-of(owner) == .union
    . constructed = construct-case(id, owner, name, arguments)
    if constructed != no-type
        = constructed
ranking.begin(arguments.shapes, arguments.types)
ranking.explicit-params(arguments.params)
. hit = ranking.dispatch-static(owner, name)
if !hit
    ranking.release()
    = type-info-call(id, owner, name, arguments)
. callee = resolve-hit(id, .call-static, arguments.syntax, .function-not-found, hit, name, 0, no-type, arguments.piped)
ranking.release()
if callee == no-instance
    = invalid-type
= demand-return(callee, id)

────────────────────
_ relates-types Bool
    - name Atom

name.text == "compare" || name.text == "compare-unified"

────────────────────
_ do type-info-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - about TypeId
    - name Atom
    - arguments Arguments

. relates = relates-types(name)
if relates && arguments.types.length == 1
    if types.intrinsic-of(arguments.types[0]) != .type-info
        frame.diagnose(arguments.syntax[0], .stated, program.store-atom("Invalid argument"))
        = invalid-type
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(about)
. info = types.class-named-with-args(frame.module, types.type-info-atom!, mark)
ranking.begin(arguments.shapes, arguments.types)
ranking.explicit-params(arguments.params)
. hit = ranking.dispatch-method(info, name)
. callee = resolve-hit(id, .call-method, arguments.syntax, .function-not-found, hit, name, 0, no-type, arguments.piped)
ranking.release()
if callee == no-instance
    = invalid-type
if relates && arguments.types.length == 1
    . other = class-arg(types, arguments.types[0], 0)
    facts.record-relation(frame.instance, id, about, other, name.text == "compare-unified")
    note-relation(id, about, other, name.text == "compare-unified")
if relates
    = types.type-row(.type-relation)
= demand-return(callee, id)

────────────────────
_ do construct-case TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - owner TypeId
    - name Atom
    - arguments Arguments

. cases = types.completions[owner].cases
for offset in 0 .. < cases.count
    . fact = types.cases[cases.start + offset]
    if fact.name && fact.name! == name
        . plan = OperatorPlan.plan-case
        if fact.type != no-type && !fact.is-default
            plan = construct-payload(fact.type, arguments)
        facts.set-constant(frame.instance, id, ConstantFact(offset, 0.0, null, false), plan)
        = owner
= no-type

────────────────────
_ do construct-payload OperatorPlan
    - payload TypeId
    - arguments Arguments

` A case of a tuple type takes the tuple's fields as its arguments, or the tuple itself; a case
` of any other type takes that one value. The plan says which.
. kind = types.intrinsic-of(payload)
. whole = arguments.types.length == 1 && arguments.types[0] == payload
if (kind != .tuple && kind != .struct) || whole
    if arguments.types.length == 1
        . site = arguments.syntax[0]
        note-context-cast(site, payload, .cast-argument)
        conversions.convert
            - site
            - site
            - payload-argument(arguments, 0, payload)
            - payload
            - .reason-argument
    = .plan-case
. position = 0
for field in types.properties-of(payload)
    if field.storage-kind == .storage-eager && position < arguments.types.length
        . expected = field.type
        if expected == no-type
            expected = host!.demand-member(field, payload, field.name)
        . site = arguments.syntax[position]
        note-context-cast(site, expected, .cast-argument)
        conversions.convert
            - site
            - site
            - payload-argument(arguments, position, expected)
            - expected
            - .reason-argument
        position += 1
= .plan-case-fields

────────────────────
+ do payload-argument TypeId
    - arguments Arguments
    - position Size
    - expected TypeId

` The type of an argument given for what a case holds, or what an event publishes. A case
` named by its symbol alone is a case of the type expected of it, as one given to a function
` is.
. given = arguments.types[position]
. shape = arguments.shapes[position]
. symbol = shape.symbol
if !symbol || !host
    = given
if shape.other-symbol
    . target = if types.is-optional(expected) then types.optional-inner(expected) else expected
    if symbols-type(types, program, target, shape) == invalid-type
        = given
    host!.note-symbol-choice(target, argument-expr(arguments.syntax[position]))
    = target
. owner = contextual-symbol(types, relations, expected, symbol, frame.module)
if owner == invalid-type || owner == no-type
    = given
. site = argument-site(arguments.syntax[position])
facts.set-node-type(frame.instance, site, owner)
host!.note-enum-case(owner, symbol, site)
if keeps-symbol(site, owner, expected, symbol)
    settle-later(site, symbol)
= owner

────────────────────
+ keeps-symbol Bool
    - site SyntaxId
    - owner TypeId
    - expected TypeId
    - name Atom
    - explicit Bool = false

` Whether a case named by its symbol alone, where it is cast to the type expected of it, stays of
` no one type as the reference keeps it: of the type its name alone gives, cast to a type without
` the case that it converts to, other than by a method of its own, as an object of a class
` becomes text. An explicit cast keeps it though it does not convert.
|? !(frame.tree.nodes[site] is .node-symbol) || owner == invalid-type || owner == no-type
    false
|? target == owner || target == invalid-type || target == no-type || generic-target
    false
|? host && symbol-type(types, program, target, name) != invalid-type
    false
|? owner != symbol-class(types, frame.module, name)
    false
|? !relation-legal(relation)
    explicit
|? relation.kind == .relation-string-cast && types.intrinsic-of(owner) == .class
    false
??
    unconverted && relation.kind != .relation-common-converter

.. target = if types.is-optional(expected) then types.optional-inner(expected) else expected
.. relation = relations.compare(owner, target, false, false, null, frame.module)
.. unconverted = relation.kind != .relation-converter && relation.kind != .relation-fromverter
.. generic-target = types.completions[target].has-variables

────────────────────
+ do settle-later
    - site SyntaxId
    - name Atom

` Notes a case named by its symbol alone that nothing settles, to report once the instance is
` typed (`report-unsettled-cases`): the reference reports one only after it has compiled
` everything else.
unsettled-sites += site
unsettled-names += name

────────────────────
+ do leave-unfound
    - site SyntaxId

` Notes a case named by its symbol alone that no type the module can name has, taken as one of
` the program's types that has it (`program-symbol-class`) until the type expected of it settles
` it (`settle-unfound`).
if unfound-sites.find(site) == null
    unfound-sites += site

────────────────────
+ do settle-unfound
    - site SyntaxId

. found = unfound-sites.find(site)
if found != null
    -= unfound-sites[found .. < found + 1]

────────────────────
+ do report-unsettled-cases

` Reports each case noted by `settle-later` that several types have, in the order noted, and
` each that no type the module can name has and nothing settled (`leave-unfound`), as the
` reference reports one only after it has compiled everything else.
for position in 0 .. < unsettled-sites.length
    ambiguous-case(unsettled-sites[position], unsettled-names[position])
for site in unfound-sites
    frame.diagnose(site, .stated, program.store-atom("Case not found"))
unsettled-sites.clear()
unsettled-names.clear()
unfound-sites.clear()

────────────────────
+ do ambiguous-case Bool
    - site SyntaxId
    - name Atom

` Reports a case named by its symbol alone that several types the module can name have, where
` nothing settles which type's it is. Says whether it reported one.
. owners [TypeId]
symbol-owners(types, frame.module, name, owners)
if owners.length < 2
    = false
. names [String]
for owner in owners
    names += owner-name(owner)
. sorted [String] = sort(names)
. listed = ""
for shown in sorted
    if listed.length != 0
        listed += ", "
    listed += "'$shown'"
frame.diagnose
    - site
    - .stated
    - program.store-atom("Case '.${name.text}' is ambiguous between $listed")
= true

────────────────────
_ owner-name String
    - type TypeId

match types.rows[type]
    | .type-class(row)
        class-name(program, row.module, row.decl)
    ??
        type-short-name(types, type)

────────────────────
+ do construction TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - callable SyntaxId
    - class-module ModuleId
    - class-decl DeclId
    - arguments Arguments

if is-tuple-class(class-module, class-decl)
    facts.set-plan(frame.instance, id, .plan-tuple)
    = tuple-of-arguments(arguments)
. receiver = construction-receiver(callable, class-module, class-decl)
if receiver == invalid-type
    . missing = types.missing-type(frame.module, frame.tree, callable, frame.env)
    if missing != 0
        frame.diagnose(missing, .stated, program.store-atom("Type not found"))
    else
        frame.diagnose(id, .not-supported)
    = invalid-type
if is-this-callable(callable)
    = construction-on(id, receiver, arguments, false, callable)
= construction-on(id, receiver, arguments, true, callable)

────────────────────
+ do construction-on TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - receiver TypeId
    - arguments Arguments
    - by-name Bool = true
    - missing-site SyntaxId = 0
    - bound Bool = false
    - explicit Bool = false

` A call of a type. Where the call is of a binding, a constructor given fewer arguments than
` it declares is partial, so its defaults do not fill them, as TypeScript dispatches a binding.
` With `explicit`, the type parameters of the arguments are the constructor's own.
types.complete(receiver)
ranking.begin(arguments.shapes, arguments.types)
ranking.bound-call = bound
if explicit
    ranking.explicit-params(arguments.params)
. hit = ranking.dispatch-constructor(receiver, by-name)
if !hit && arguments.curried && ranking.partial
    = bind-partial(.bound-constructor, receiver, arguments)
if hit && arguments.curried && types.completions[hit.receiver].has-variables
    . module = hit.module
    . decl = hit.decl
    ranking.release()
    = bind-values(.bound-constructor, receiver, arguments, module, decl)
. form = if by-name then CallForm.call-constructor else CallForm.call-this-constructor
. site = if missing-site != 0 then missing-site else id
match? frame.tree.nodes[site]
    | .node-type-arguments(named)
        site = named.base
if hit
    . fills = false
    for shape in arguments.shapes
        if shape.is-property
            fills = true
            break
    if fills || arguments.slots.length != 0 || arguments.context != U32.max
        constructing = Construction
            - hit.module
            - hit.decl
            - hit.receiver
            - fills
            - arguments.context
            - arguments.slots
            - arguments.builders
. diagnosed = facts.diagnostics.length
. callee = resolve-hit(id, form, arguments.syntax, .constructor-not-found, hit, null, site, no-type, arguments.piped)
constructing = Construction()
ranking.release()
if callee == no-instance
    if !hit
        explain-rows(receiver, arguments, by-name, diagnosed)
    = invalid-type
. constructed = if !types.completions[receiver].has-variables then receiver else hit!.receiver
. deferred = false
if host
    host.demand(callee)
if by-name && types.intrinsic-of(constructed) == .class
    frame.check-allocates(id)
if host
    if !instances.errors-known(callee)
        . running = instances.rows[callee].state == .instance-in-progress
        if frame.surround.catch-depth != 0 || running || converts-literal(hit!, arguments)
            host!.demand-errors(callee)
        else
            defer-outgoing(callee, id)
            deferred = true
. signature = instances.signatures[callee]
. returned = signature.returns
if signature.return-state != .return-pending && returned != no-type && returned != invalid-type
    constructed = returned
if signature.errors.count != 0 && !deferred
    if frame.surround.catch-depth != 0
        = result-type(types, constructed, error-items(signature))
    if converts-literal(hit!, arguments)
        instances.mark-may-panic(frame.instance)
        conversions.demand-error-report()
        facts.set-plan(frame.instance, id, .plan-literal-conversion)
        = constructed
    for offset in 0 .. < signature.errors.count
        note-outgoing(instances.signature-types[signature.errors.start + offset], id)
    facts.mark-propagates(frame.instance, id)
= constructed

────────────────────
_ do converts-literal Bool
    - hit Hit
    - arguments Arguments

` A call of a type with one text written in source, which a function the type declares
` converts, is a conversion of the text: where it fails outside a catch it panics rather than
` raising from the function it is written in.
if arguments.syntax.length != 1 || arguments.shapes.length != 1
    = false
if arguments.shapes[0].name || !conversions.is-text-literal(arguments.syntax[0])
    = false
match? program.modules[hit.module].decls[hit.decl]
    | .decl-fromverter
        = true
= false

────────────────────
+ do error-items Size
    - signature InstanceSignature

` Pushes the errors a signature raises onto the scratch types, answering the mark below them.
. mark = scratch.types.mark
for offset in 0 .. < signature.errors.count
